title: Curl Download to User-Writable Directory
status: experimental
description: Detects curl.exe downloading a file from a remote URL into a user-writable directory such as AppData or Temp. Observed in the EtherRAT intrusion where a script used curl to download a portable Node.js runtime into the user's Temp folder.
references:
    - https://thedfirreport.com/2026/05/11/flash-alert-etherrat-and-tuktuk-c2-end-in-the-gentleman-ransomware/
author: Sümeyra Yüksel
date: 2026/10/21
tags:
    - attack.command-and-control
    - attack.t1105
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
    service
detection:
    selection_img:
        - Image|endswith: '\curl.exe'
        - OriginalFileName: 'curl.exe'
    selection_url:
        CommandLine|contains: 'http'
    selection_path:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - '\AppData\'
            - '\Local\'
            - '\Temp\'
    condition: all of selection_*
fields:
    - ParentImage
    - Image
    - CommandLine
    - User
falsepositives:
    - Software update scripts or developers legitimately downloading files with curl
level: low
